  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Mongolia 2023 &#x2013; October visit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to the many occurrences of heavy rainfall in July and August 2023, the flood water levels of Tuul and Selbe rivers have reached a historic high. The city of Ulaanbaatar has faced multiple large-scale floods and water disasters, more than 128,000 people were directly affected.Ulaanbaatar is highly prone to urban flooding in the future. This has a detrimental impact on the urban environment and transport infrastructure in Ulaanbaatar.The World Bank (WB) is highly engaged in the space of flood risk mitigation and drainage, and is discussing financing opportunities with the Municipality of Ulaanbaatar (MoUB).Hence, a workshop is being organised by the WB and MoUB to detail next steps in October 2023. It is proposed to ask an expert from the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) to join the workshop and to present concepts such as Room for the River.</narrative>
  </description>
